-- DB update 2026_09_10_09 -> 2026_09_10_10
-- Arcane Mage rework (docs/arcane-mage-rework-design.md) - Magic Absorption (1,0) fix, found
-- while building the Phase 3 (0,1)-(10,1) work and confirmed via a live worldserver boot log
-- warning: "Effect ... did not match dbc effect data - handler bound to hook OnEffectProc of
-- AuraScript won't be executed" for spell_mage_magic_absorption on 29441/29444/200075.
--
-- Root cause: that pre-existing script implements real stock Magic Absorption's "restore mana
-- when a spell is fully resisted" clause (SPELL_MAGE_MAGIC_ABSORPTION_MANA = 29442), which isn't
-- one of this rework's 3 design clauses for (1,0) at all (dmg done%, dmg taken%, Mana Gem bonus%) -
-- it's vestigial from the Rows 0-3 batch replacing this talent's content wholesale onto the same
-- talent id/slot. The design's third clause ("Increases the mana you gain from Mana Gems by
-- 15/30/45%") was correctly identified as unbuilt back in that batch (see this file's own CSV
-- notes), explicitly deferred to Phase 3 - but never made it onto the design doc's tracked
-- "Deferred to Phase 3" list, so none of this session's 4 Phase 3 batches picked it up. Found only
-- because the boot log's warning pointed at the real underlying cause instead of just the symptom.
--
-- That same deferral note incorrectly assumed Mana Gems are SPELLFAMILY_GENERIC and would need "a
-- different mechanism" - checking the real data shows both Conjure Mana Gem (759) and this fork's
-- own Mana Gem cast spell (200005, "Restore Mana", Frost Mage rework) are SPELLFAMILY_MAGE, so a
-- plain classmask-scoped SpellMod reaches them fine after all.
--
-- Fix: 200005 gets a fresh identity classmask (SpellClassSet 0 -> 3, dword3 bit 16 - previously
-- unused, same "give a custom spell its own identity bit" pattern as Brilliance Aura/Arcane
-- Overload/Temporal Convergence this session). Magic Absorption (29441/29444/200075) gets a new
-- effect3 (previously unused): SPELLMOD_ALL_EFFECTS (misc_value 8) classmask-scoped to that bit,
-- 15/30/45% - the real mechanism, not a guess (SPELLMOD_ALL_EFFECTS scales a target spell's
-- effects regardless of their type, matching a native SPELL_EFFECT_ENERGIZE_PCT effect exactly).
--
-- generate.py clean (zero lint WARNINGs). No C++ change - pure data fix, no rebuild needed, only
-- db-import + a worldserver restart to reload spell_dbc.

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (29441, 29444, 200005, 200075);
